From fd2aff2ab6400ccadd61b01fbb4b7086a3231796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bubunuh <76405364+bubunuh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:51:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/21] HandleBinder: one alignment for all units, creation as
 a window

Three changes to how units are tied to handles, and what an untied unit means:

- WC3V's own ties are a small bonus inside the alignment, no longer kept
  outright. Kept, the ones it made out of creation order (e.g. the Rifleman
  trained first tied to the later handle) block the alignment of every unit
  around them.
- A unit's creation is a window: from its queue time + build time up to WC3V's
  training time. WC3V's queues also hold orders the game refused (no gold, no
  food), so its training time is often late.
- A handle can't be a unit made after the first sighting of any handle the
  game allocated after it (any player's): madeBy(counter), a much tighter
  bound than the handle's own first sighting.
- Only handles the player gave orders to, grouped or box-selected with other
  units are candidates; one only ever clicked on alone is an enemy's, a
  creep, a shop.

A trained unit the binder could not tie is never shown by the lists; two
minutes after its training DeathInference counts it as never made (source
'unlisted'): its path, if any, came from orders to a handle that is another
unit's.

Dev games: army value error 115 -> 114 (Human 102 -> 88, Orc 97 -> 72;
Undead 143 -> 159, Night Elf 120 -> 136).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
